A locally usual measure algebra is a probability measure space that fulfils certain conditions derived from total disorder on a specific subset. A measure algebra is considered locally usual if it can be obtained by modifying a totally disorder measure on a particular subset. This paper classifies locally usual measure algebras developed from bounded measure algebras. It is demonstrated that such classifications yield an equivalent structure to the Stepanov ultrasoft compact open ideal in 2-wonderful spaces. Additionally, an example is provided of a locally usual measure algebra that cannot be obtained from a totally disorder measure on a subset. Finally, a question regarding the classification of all locally usual measure algebras is posed. \par \textbf{Mathematics Subject Classification:} Primary 28S40, Secondary 54H15, 54J10, 03E15, 03G25. \textbf{Keywords:} measure algebras, totally disorder measures, locally usual measure algebras, bounded measure algebras, 2-wonderful spaces, Stepanov ultrasoft compact open ideal. {\small \vspace{7.5cm} \hrulefill \small S.\;G.\;Gonz\'alez}\end{document}

